      "purpose": "A fixed-format ILE RPG program (XEXECPPC2) that acts as a script executor engine on IBM i. It reads script lines from a source file (xScript) via embedded SQL cursors, substitutes positional parameter values (%0..%8), buffers lines until a semicolon terminator, then classifies and dispatches each statement as either an SQL DDL/DML command (executed via EXECUTE IMMEDIATE), a special control directive (MONITOR, END-MONITOR, STOP, SELF-SUBMIT), or an IBM i CL command (executed via QCMDEXC). It logs execution progress and errors to an xLog table using embedded SQL INSERT, supports a monitor mode to suppress error-stops, and can self-submit the job via SBMJOB for batch execution. It is called as a subprogram with parameters including a script name, library, file, parameter values array, call recursion level, and job type.",
